# ChkPnt Flutter Development Rules - Production-Ready Architecture

## 🎯 Core Principles

- **🚨 CRITICAL: Always use explicit colours** - Never rely on Material Design defaults (Android 13 compatibility)
- **🚫 NEVER RUN THE APP** - The developer will always run the app themselves
- **Always use British English spellings** (colour, centre, organisation, etc.)
- **Extract Complex Build Methods** using `_buildXXX()` pattern
- **Separate Business Logic** from UI rendering
- **Use Centralised Styling** from `lib/styles/`
- **Follow Streaming Architecture** with Riverpod providers
- **Test Everything** - All new functionality must have comprehensive tests
- **Quality Assurance** - Always run Flutter Analyze and tests after changes

## 🔄 State Management - Riverpod Streaming Architecture

### 🎯 Core State Management Principles
- **All data sources use streams** for reactive updates
- **Repository pattern** with abstract interfaces for easy backend swapping  
- **AsyncValue handling** throughout with proper loading/error states
- **Dependency injection** via Riverpod providers
- **No runtime provider initialization** - use Family providers for context-dependent state

### Current Implementation Pattern
```dart
// Repository provider - swap storage implementations easily
@riverpod
GameRepository gameRepository(Ref ref) {
  final storageService = ref.read(storageServiceProvider);
  final repository = DriftGameRepository(storageService);
  ref.onDispose(() => repository.dispose());
  return repository;
}

// Streaming data provider
@riverpod
Stream<List<GameItem>> gamesStream(Ref ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(gameRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.watchGames();
}

// Current state provider for UI consumption
@riverpod
class GameList extends _$GameList {
  @override
  List<GameItem> build() {
    final gamesAsync = ref.watch(gamesStreamProvider);
    return gamesAsync.when(
      data: (games) => games,
      loading: () => [],
      error: (error, stack) => [],
    );
  }

  // CRUD operations
  Future<void> createGame({...}) async { /* implementation */ }
  Future<void> updateGame(GameItem updatedGame) async { /* implementation */ }
  Future<void> removeGame(GameId gameId) async { /* implementation */ }
}

// Derived providers - automatically update when base data changes
@riverpod
List<GameItem> gamesByStatus(Ref ref, GameStatus status) {
  final games = ref.watch(gameListProvider);
  return games.where((game) => game.status == status).toList();
}
```

### 🎯 Family Provider Rules (Critical for Context-Dependent State)
- **Always use Family** for screen-specific state instead of runtime initialization
- **Create context classes** with proper `==` and `hashCode` implementation
- **Initialize context in initState()** not provider state
- **Use simple `pump()`** in tests instead of `pumpAndSettle()`

```dart
// Context class for Family parameters
class GameEditContext {
  final bool isAddMode;
  final GameItem? game;

  const GameEditContext({required this.isAddMode, this.game});

  @override
  bool operator ==(Object other) => 
    identical(this, other) ||
    other is GameEditContext &&
    isAddMode == other.isAddMode &&
    game == other.game;

  @override
  int get hashCode => Object.hash(isAddMode, game);
}

// Family provider - eliminates initialization issues
@riverpod
class GameEditState extends _$GameEditState {
  @override
  GameEditFormState build(GameEditContext context) {
    if (context.isAddMode) {
      return const GameEditFormState.empty();
    } else {
      return GameEditFormState.fromGame(context.game!);
    }
  }
}
```

## 💾 Data Layer - Drift/SQLite Production Implementation

### Current Repository Implementation
- **Full SQLite persistence** with Drift ORM
- **Streaming queries** with automatic UI updates
- **ACID transactions** for data integrity
- **Database migrations** for schema evolution
- **Backup and restore** functionality

```dart
// Abstract interface allows easy backend swapping
abstract class GameRepository {
  Stream<List<GameItem>> watchGames();           // Streaming data
  Future<List<GameItem>> getAllGames();          // One-time access
  Future<GameItem> createGame(GameItem game);    // CRUD operations
  Future<GameItem> updateGame(GameItem game);
  Future<void> deleteGame(GameId gameId);
  Future<String> exportDatabaseToJson();        // Backup functionality
  Future<void> importFromJson(String jsonString);
}

// Current production implementation
class DriftGameRepository implements GameRepository {
  // Full SQLite implementation with streaming, transactions, migrations
  // Handles database integrity, proper error handling, and streaming updates
}
```

## 🎨 Styling Architecture - Critical Android 13 Compatibility

### 🚨 **NEVER** Rely on Material Design Defaults
**CRITICAL RULE**: Android 13 and older versions handle Material Design theming differently, causing text and UI elements to become invisible. Always use **explicit colour and style declarations**.

#### ❌ **FORBIDDEN PATTERNS** - These cause Android 13 invisibility:
```dart
// NEVER use theme-based styling
Text('Hello', style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyMedium)
Container(color: Theme.of(context).cardColor)
Card(child: Text('Hello')) // Background colour undefined

// NEVER use TextStyle without explicit colours
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16)) // No colour = invisible text
```

#### ✅ **REQUIRED PATTERNS** - Always use explicit styling:
```dart
// ALWAYS use explicit colours from AppColors
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(
  fontSize: 16,
  color: AppColors.primaryText, // Explicit colour required
  fontWeight: FontWeight.w500,
))

// ALWAYS specify Card colours explicitly
Card(
  color: Colors.white, // Explicit background
  child: Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(color: AppColors.primaryText)),
)

// ALWAYS use explicit button styling
ElevatedButton(
  onPressed: onPressed,
  style: ElevatedButton.styleFrom(
    backgroundColor: AppColors.primaryPurple,
    foregroundColor: Colors.white,
    disabledBackgroundColor: Colors.grey[300],
    disabledForegroundColor: Colors.grey[600],
  ),
  child: Text('Click'),
)
```

### Current Styling Implementation
```dart
// Centralised styling in lib/styles/
import 'package:chkpnt/styles/game_card_styles.dart';
import 'package:chkpnt/styles/global_styles.dart';

Container(
  decoration: GameCardStyles.gameCardDecoration,
  child: Text('Title', style: TextStyle(colour: AppColours.primaryText)),
)
```

## 🏗️ Widget Architecture Patterns

### Screen Organization Rules
- **Feature-based screens** in `screens/[feature]/`
- **Screen-specific widgets** in `screens/[feature]/widgets/`  
- **Animations** in `screens/[feature]/widgets/animations/`
- **Truly reusable components** in `shared/widgets/`

### 🚨 **CRITICAL: Avoid Excessive Nesting and Embedded Styles**

#### ❌ **FORBIDDEN PATTERNS** - These create unmaintainable code:
```dart
// NEVER have deeply nested widget trees in build methods
Widget _buildContent() {
  return Column(
    children: [
      Expanded(
        child: SingleChildScrollView(
          child: Column(
            children: [
              Row(
                children: [
                  Expanded(
                    child: Column(
                      children: [
                        Container(
                          child: Row(
                            children: [
                              // More nesting...
                            ],
                          ),
                        ),
                      ],
                    ),
                  ),
                ],
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ],
  );
}

// NEVER use embedded styles with hardcoded values
AppBar(
  title: Text(
    'Title',
    style: TextStyle(
      color: Colors.black87,        // ❌ Hardcoded colour
      fontSize: 18,                 // ❌ Magic number
      fontWeight: FontWeight.w600,  // ❌ Hardcoded style
    ),
  ),
)

// NEVER use magic numbers in layouts
const SizedBox(width: 20),  // ❌ Magic number
const SizedBox(height: 16), // ❌ Magic number
```

#### ✅ **REQUIRED PATTERNS** - Always extract widgets and use centralised styling:
```dart
// ALWAYS extract complex nested structures into separate widgets
Widget _buildContent() {
  return Column(
    children: [
      Expanded(child: _buildScrollableContent()),
      _buildBottomSection(),
    ],
  );
}

Widget _buildScrollableContent() {
  return SingleChildScrollView(
    child: Column(
      children: [
        _buildHeaderSection(),
        _buildMainContent(),
      ],
    ),
  );
}

Widget _buildHeaderSection() {
  return Row(
    children: [
      _buildImageSection(),
      _buildInfoSection(),
    ],
  );
}

// ALWAYS use centralised styles for all styling
AppBar(
  title: Text(
    'Title',
    style: EditScreenStyles.appBarTitleStyle, // ✅ Centralised style
  ),
)

// ALWAYS use named constants for spacing
const SizedBox(width: EditScreenStyles.horizontalSpacing),  // ✅ Named constant
const SizedBox(height: EditScreenStyles.verticalSpacing),   // ✅ Named constant
```

### Extract Complex Build Methods Pattern
```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Scaffold(
    body: SafeArea(
      child: _buildContent(),
    ),
  );
}

Widget _buildContent() {
  return Column(
    children: [
      _buildHeader(),
      Expanded(child: _buildGamesList()),
      _buildBottomActions(),
    ],
  );
}

Widget _buildHeader() {
  return Container(
    padding: MainScreenStyles.headerPadding,
    child: _buildSearchBar(),
  );
}
```

### Current Screen Features
- **Main Dashboard** - Game overview with status-based sections, quick actions (play, complete, edit), search and platform filtering, animated transitions and interactions
- **Backlog Management** - Advanced sorting options (alphabetical, date added, platform), platform-specific sections with expansion controls, bulk operations and batch editing, smart filtering and search
- **Wishlist & Orders** - Track desired games and pre-orders, price tracking integration (planned), release date management, platform-specific organisation
- **Profile & Statistics** - Visual progress charts with FL Chart, gaming statistics and insights, progress tracking over time, achievement-style milestones
- **Game Editing** - Full CRUD operations with form validation, image selection (camera, gallery, remote URL), platform management with custom options, animated form transitions
- **Onboarding** - User onboarding flow with subscription options and modern overlay design
- **Splash Screen** - Initial app loading with branding

## 🧪 Testing Strategy - Production-Ready Coverage

### Current Test Architecture
```
test/
├── models/                        # Data model tests
├── providers/                     # State management tests
├── repositories/                  # Data layer tests
├── services/                      # Business logic tests
├── screens/                       # Screen and widget tests
│   ├── main/widgets/             # Main screen components
│   ├── backlog/                  # Backlog screen tests
│   ├── edit/widgets/animations/  # Edit screen animations
│   └── profile/widgets/          # Profile visualizations
├── shared/widgets/               # Reusable component tests
├── test_helpers.dart             # Shared testing utilities
├── core_functionality_test.dart  # Core feature integration
└── business_logic_test.dart      # Business rule validation
```

### Testing Requirements
- **All new widgets** must have corresponding test files
- **State management** tests for all providers and business logic
- **Data persistence** tests for repository operations
- **UI interactions** tests for user workflows
- **Error handling** tests for network failures and edge cases

### Test Implementation Pattern
```dart
testWidgets('GameCard displays correctly', (tester) async {
  final container = TestHelpers.createTestContainer();
  
  await tester.pumpWidget(
    UncontrolledProviderScope(
      container: container,
      child: MaterialApp(
        home: GameCard(game: TestHelpers.createTestGame()),
      ),
    ),
  );

  expect(find.byType(GameCard), findsOneWidget);
  expect(find.text('Test Game'), findsOneWidget);
  
  container.dispose();
});
```

## 🚀 Development Workflow

### Quality Gates
1. **Flutter Analyze** - No warnings allowed
2. **All Tests Pass** - Comprehensive test coverage
3. **Manual Android 13 Testing** - UI visibility verification
4. **Code Generation** - `dart run build_runner build` for changes

### Pre-Commit Checklist
```bash
# 1. Code quality check
flutter analyze

# 2. Run comprehensive tests
flutter test

# 3. Regenerate code if models/providers changed
dart run build_runner build

# 4. Verify coverage
flutter test --coverage
```

### Adding New Features
1. **Define models** in `lib/models/` with Freezed
2. **Create providers** in `lib/providers/` with streaming
3. **Implement services** in `lib/services/` for business logic
4. **Build screen widgets** in `screens/[feature]/widgets/`
5. **Add comprehensive tests** for all components
6. **Use centralised styling** from `lib/styles/`
7. **Run quality checks** - analyze and test

## 🔧 Technical Stack Requirements

### State Management
- **Riverpod 2.5.1** with code generation
- **AsyncValue handling** for loading/error states
- **Family providers** for context-dependent state

### Data Persistence  
- **Drift 2.18.0** for type-safe SQLite operations
- **Stream-based queries** for reactive UI updates
- **Database migrations** for schema evolution

### UI Framework
- **Flutter 3.7.2+** with Material Design 3
- **Responsive layouts** for portrait and landscape orientations
- **FL Chart** for profile statistics visualization
- **Image handling** with local and remote image support

### Data Models
- **Freezed 2.5.2** for immutable data classes with code generation
- **JSON serialization** for data export/import and backup functionality
- **Type safety** with compile-time validation and null safety
- **UUID generation** for unique game identifiers

## 📋 Code Quality Standards

### Mandatory Patterns
- **British English spellings** throughout (colour, centre, organisation)
- **Explicit colours** in all UI components (Android 13 compatibility)
- **Streaming providers** for all data access
- **Comprehensive error handling** with user-friendly messages
- **Family providers** for context-dependent state
- **Build method extraction** using `_buildXXX()` pattern

### Forbidden Patterns
- **Theme.of(context)** usage for colours or text styles
- **Runtime provider initialization** in widget lifecycle
- **Magic numbers** - use named constants from styles
- **Inline styling** - use centralised style classes
- **Missing test coverage** for new functionality
- **Excessive widget nesting** - extract complex structures into separate widgets
- **Embedded styles** - never use inline TextStyle with hardcoded colours/fonts
- **Deep widget trees** - break down complex layouts into smaller, focused widgets

